---
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = '17 September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms | Canopy"
  description="The terms that apply to the Canopy website. Platform use is governed by a separate agreement."
>
  <div class="legal">
    <div class="shell legal__inner">
      <p class="section-kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p class="legal__lead">
        These terms cover <strong>canopy.ag</strong>, our marketing website. Use of the Canopy
        platform is governed by the written agreement between Canopy and your organization,
        which takes precedence over anything on this page.
      </p>
      <p class="legal__meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>Using this site</h2>
      <p>
        Read it, share it, quote it. What you may not do is interfere with it: no attempts to
        breach or probe its security, no scraping that degrades it for others, and no using
        the demo form to send unsolicited commercial messages or anything unlawful.
      </p>

      <h2>What is on it</h2>
      <p>
        The content here describes what Canopy does and where the product is going. Some of
        it describes work in progress. It is written in good faith and kept current, but it
        is not a warranty, a specification, or a commitment to ship a particular capability
        on a particular date. Nothing here forms a contract.
      </p>

      <h2>Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        Canopy owns this site, its text, and its marks. The open-source components it is
        built from carry their own licences. Anything you send us through the demo form
        stays yours; you are giving us permission to read it and reply, nothing more.
      </p>

      <h2>Links out</h2>
      <p>
        Where we link to someone else, we are pointing at something useful, not vouching for
        it. What happens on their site is theirs to govern.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        This site is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, Canopy is not liable
        for loss arising from relying on the content of this website. Nothing here limits
        liability that cannot lawfully be limited, and nothing here limits or replaces the
        obligations in a signed customer agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The date above says when we last did.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions go to <a href="mailto:hello@canopy.ag">hello@canopy.ag</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: 8rem 0 6rem;
  }
  .legal__inner {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
  }
  .legal p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.62);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .legal__lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75) !important;
  }
  .legal__meta {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35) !important;
    margin-bottom: 2rem !important;
  }
  .legal a {
    color: #22c55e;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .legal a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .legal strong {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  }
  .legal ul {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.62);
    line-height: 1.7;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
